# Copy to .env.local if you want to change anything. Nothing here is required:
# with no settings the login rule decides where the phone connects from the
# username alone (1004@dave.mosaicvoice.net -> the Mosaic Voice edge).
#
# Vite builds every VITE_* value into the page's JavaScript, so never put the
# SIP password here; it is typed into the login page.

# Override where the phone connects, for a setup where the WebSocket host and
# the SIP realm differ. The phone then connects to wss://<host>/api/asterisk/ws
# and uses <host> as the SIP domain whatever the username's domain says. There
# are no fields for these on the login page.
# VITE_WAZO_HOST=wazo.example.com

# Optional overrides
# VITE_SIP_WS_URL=wss://wazo.example.com/api/asterisk/ws
# VITE_SIP_DOMAIN=wazo.example.com

# Optional: prefill the username field, e.g. 1004@dave.mosaicvoice.net.
# VITE_SIP_USERNAME=

# ICE servers, comma-separated. Unset uses Google's public STUN server; set it empty for none.
# TURN credentials set here end up in the shipped JavaScript: use short-lived ones.
# VITE_ICE_SERVERS=stun:stun.l.google.com:19302,turn:turn.example.com:3478
# VITE_TURN_USERNAME=
# VITE_TURN_CREDENTIAL=

# Log every SIP message to the browser console (handy while testing).
# VITE_SIP_TRACE=true
